# 07 · The evening loop: log tonight, plan tomorrow, get checked in on
goal: Learn Assembly
book: Programming from the Ground Up
# At night, say what you did today. Each line is saved as done.
did: Finished the chapter 2 exercises
did: Read about the stack
# Then plan tomorrow. Tomorrow is the default day.
plan: Read chapter 3
plan: Write notes on registers
# Other days work too: monday, 2026-10-12, +3d ...
plan monday: Review stack frames
:plan
# The next evening your OS scheduler runs `idios remind` (see :schedule) and sends a
# desktop notification. When you open IDIOS it offers this review.
# Here, "plan today" stands in for "what I planned yesterday".
plan today: Read chapter 3 again
plan today: Summarise the stack
:review
# y = done, n = not yet (moves to tomorrow), s = skip
y
n
:plan
# Everything is searchable, and the review was saved as a note.
:search chapter
:schedule
